[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://data/loot/EmbermarketCaravanGear.tres" id="4_pool"]

; Sera of the Long Road (Phase 38L) - one of two travelling merchants on this square, in one day in
; five, and the only shop in the Ember Crown that sells goods from another realm. Her Frostfang pelts and
; her southern spice are the market's evidence that there IS somewhere else.
;
; ⚠️ SHE IS MOUNTED WITH A VendorComponent, NOT A CONVERSATION, AND THAT IS FORCED. DialogueSession
; evaluates ShopOpen/ShopClosed through ShopHours.IsOpenAt alone - hours, not presence - and the only
; thing that hides an away merchant and kills her collider is VendorComponent.ApplyPresence. A traveller
; wired through a dialogue choice would stand at her cart every day of the cycle with a working trade
; line, which is 38J's mechanic inverted. Hesk took the same route for the same reason.
; ⚠️ The cost of that: her ShopId lives in embermarket.tscn and --validate cannot read it. A typo gives
; NO PROMPT AT ALL rather than an error.
;
; ⚠️ NOT ONE CONSUMABLE ON HER SHELVES. --validate rejects a consumable sold only by travelling shops:
; hours are a wait a player can sleep off, but a merchant who may not be in town is a coin flip against
; the calendar, and a player out of rations cannot sleep their way to one.
;
; Empty AcceptedTags - she buys anything, like Hesk. Aldreth is still the settlement's mandated resident
; catch-all; a traveller cannot be it.
;
; Empty FactionId, which also means none of her rows may carry a standing gate: --validate rejects one on
; a shop that prices by no faction, because the window falls back to Neutral and the shelf never opens.
;
; A 5-day cycle at offset 2 against Quill's 3-day at offset 0: they share the square only one day in
; fifteen. Two travellers who always arrive together are one traveller.

